hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"312","I am Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala al-San’ani, and Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Habib bin al-Shahid. They said: Al-Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, our father Othman, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned to him that he had been infected with a woman, either by a kiss or a touch. With a hand, or something, as if he was asking about her atonement. He said: Then God Almighty revealed: And perform prayer at the ends of the day and at the end of the night. Good deeds remove evil deeds. That is a reminder for those who remember. Surat Hud, verse 114. He said: Then the man said: Who is this? He said: “It is for those of my nation who do it.” He said: Al-San’ani narrated to us, Yazid bin Zurai’ narrated to us, Suleiman, who is Al-Tamimi, narrated to us with this chain of transmission similar to it, and he said: It was narrated by someone who narrated it. He kissed a woman, and he did not doubt, nor did he say, as if he was asking about her expiation."
"313","It is narrated by Ya’qub bin Ibrahim Al-Durqi, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, and Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I met a woman in the garden, so I hugged her to me. And I had intercourse with her, and I kissed her, and I did everything to her, except that I did not have intercourse with her, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent, and this verse was revealed: Good deeds remove evil deeds. That is a reminder for those who remember. Surah Hud, verse 114. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called him and recited it to him. Then Omar said: O Messenger of God. God, specifically for him or for all people? He said: “No, but for all people.”"
